		<r3d:repositoryName language="eng">AuScope EarthBank Platform</r3d:repositoryName>
				<r3d:repositoryUrl>https://ausgeochem.auscope.org.au/</r3d:repositoryUrl>
				<r3d:description language="eng">The AuScope EarthBank platform (formerly AusGeochem) is an easy-to-use platform for uploading, visualising, analysing and discovering georeferenced sample information and data produced by various geoscience research institutions such as universities, geological survey agencies and museums. With respect to analytical research laboratories, the AuScope EarthBank platform provides a centralised repository allowing laboratories to upload, synthesis, disseminate and publish their datasets. The intuitive user interface allows users to access publicly funded data quickly through the ability to view an area of interest, synthesise a variety of geochemical data in real-time, and extract the required data, gaining novel scientific insights through multi-method data collation. Developed in collaboration with Lithodat Pty Ltd, the platform features integrated built-in data visualisation functions, such as cumulative age histograms, age vs elevation plots, and step-heating diagrams, allowing for rapid inter-study comparisons. Data can be extracted in multiple formats for re-use in a variety of software systems, allowing for the integration of regional datasets into machine learning and AI systems.</r3d:description>
